From d914b93c50ab91e91868fe7d32c902041e23162d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:36:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] flake: drop --impure from the build commands

With emacs-overlay and the Emacs source locked as flake inputs, galago
and router evaluate in pure mode.  Neither the hourly build of galago
nor the VM command in the comment on router needs --impure any more,
and that comment no longer has a pure evaluation failure to warn of.
---
 .github/workflows/build-galago.yml | 5 +----
 flake.nix                          | 9 +++------
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build-galago.yml b/.github/workflows/build-galago.yml
index 7930cc5..eb466f5 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build-galago.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build-galago.yml
@@ -20,15 +20,12 @@ jobs:
       - name: Update flake.lock
         run: nix flake update
 
-      # Same target as `nixos-rebuild switch --flake . --impure`;
-      # `--impure` is needed because the Emacs overlay uses a bare
-      # `builtins.fetchTarball`.
+      # Same target as `nixos-rebuild switch --flake .`;
       # `--keep-going` builds the rest if one package fails, and
       # cachix's daemon pushes each successful path as it builds.
       - name: Build galago
         run: |
           nix build \
-            --impure \
             --keep-going \
             --no-link \
             ".#nixosConfigurations.galago.config.system.build.toplevel"
diff --git a/flake.nix b/flake.nix
index 76a78a5..fafc50a 100644
--- a/flake.nix
+++ b/flake.nix
@@ -164,13 +164,10 @@
           .#router` won't work, since it builds the stock
           `system.build.vm`, which boots an empty overlay root and
           ignores the disko layout entirely (no bcachefs partitions,
-          no swap, and no mounted subvolumes).  It also fails pure
-          evaluation, because importing
-          `../../systems/nixos/commons.nix` pulls in the emacs-overlay
-          `fetchTarball` without a pinned `sha256`.  Instead, build a
-          VM backed by a real disko image, which boots the actual
+          no swap, and no mounted subvolumes).  Instead, build a VM
+          backed by a real disko image, which boots the actual
           bcachefs/swap layout:
-          `$ nix build .#nixosConfigurations.router.config.system.build.vmWithDisko --impure`
+          `$ nix build .#nixosConfigurations.router.config.system.build.vmWithDisko`
         */
         router = nixosSystem-patched {
           system = "x86_64-linux";
-- 
